Step 3 of the build-up. Identical to
cloud-vms-vs-containers-what-customers-buy-2.svg (see that prompt), with
nothing moved, plus what is inside each VM:

- A's VM: the concrete stack (nginx, postgres, JRE running a spring-boot
  service) on A's own guest kernel. A's colour box wraps the whole inside of
  that VM, kernel included, to make clear A owns the complete VM and can
  modify the kernel.
- B's and C's platform VMs: a container runtime row and their own guest
  kernel below the containers.
- The footer becomes the takeaway: container customers never see a VM, yet
  each gets one (in a typical setup); the VM boundary separates customers.
